.TH z3 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
z3 \- play a version 3 Infocom story file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B z3
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.I storyfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B z3
is fweeplet, a cut-down fweep, built for version 3 of the Z-machine:
the format of most of Infocom's games from 1982 to 1987, and of many
written since with Inform.  It plays any version 3 story file and
refuses any other version with "Unsupported Z-machine version".  It
cannot read a Blorb file; the plain story has to be taken out of one
first.
.PP
The story is read from its file a page at a time rather than held in
memory, and the parts of it the game changes are kept in a temporary
file in
.BR /tmp ,
which goes when the game ends.
.PP
.BR zork1 (1)
plays Zork I with it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Tell the game it is running on a Tandy computer.  A few of Infocom's
games change some words for Tandy.
.TP
.B \-p
Answer no when a game asks whether it is running from its original
disc.
.TP
.B \-q
Accepted, and does nothing.
.SH PLAYING
There is no status line: type
.B look
or
.B score
instead.  Text is wrapped at 80 columns, and after 25 lines the game
waits at
.B [MORE]
for Return.
.PP
.B save
asks "*** Save?" for a file name, and
.B restore
asks "*** Restore?" for one.  Saved games are in this program's own
format and do not load into other interpreters.
.PP
Every game says it is release 2: the interpreter writes over the release
number in the story's header.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zork1 (1),
.BR advent (1)
